# Environment for the PUBLIC /v1 process — a different process from the
# dashboard API, with a different config file.
#
# Copy to `server/.env.public` (gitignored) and edit. Two commands read it:
#
#   npm run dev:public     the public /v1 server  (src/v1/publicIndex.ts)
#   npm run keys -- ...    the API-key CLI        (src/v1/keys/keysCli.ts)
#
# `server/.env` is the PRIVATE app's file and is NOT read here. That separation
# is the point: the private app's environment carries ENERGY_DB_PATH and
# HELIO_WRITE_TOKEN, and the public composition refuses to start if it is handed
# either kind of capability (FORBIDDEN_PUBLIC_ENV, src/v1/publicEnv.ts).

# --- API key store (ABL-300) ----------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED, and deliberately with no default.
#
# This is its OWN SQLite file. It must never be the shared energy database:
# that file is 376 GiB, is owned by the `energy-data-gathering` sibling module,
# and is opened readonly by this server — writing account and key rows into it
# would add a write path contending with ingest, in a schema we do not own.
# `resolveApiKeysDbPath` refuses to start if this path and ENERGY_DB_PATH
# resolve to the same file, and refuses the `/data/energy_dashboard.db` default
# too.
#
# There is no default because a credentials file must not land somewhere nobody
# chose. The serving process opens this readonly and requires it to exist; the
# keys CLI opens it read-write and creates it.
#
#   cd server
#   npm run keys -- accounts:create --name "Acme Energy" --plan developer
#   npm run keys -- keys:issue --account acct_... --label "prod ETL"
#
# The key is printed once and cannot be recovered: the store holds
# sha256(secret) plus the non-secret 8-character prefix. A lost key is rotated,
# never re-read.
API_KEYS_DB_PATH=C:/Code/able/data/api_keys.db

# --- Binding ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Defaults to 127.0.0.1:3002. PUBLIC_BIND_HOST exists so the bind address is
# configuration rather than a code change — but setting it to anything other
# than loopback is a network-exposure decision that needs its own
# Board-approved issue (ABL-291). This process is not deployed or exposed.
# PUBLIC_PORT=3002
# PUBLIC_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1

# --- CORS ------------------------------------------------------------------
# A comma-separated allowlist of browser origins, defaulting to EMPTY = deny.
# Unlike the private app (`origin: true` + `credentials: true`), nothing is
# reflected back. Non-browser callers — curl, a server-side SDK — are
# unaffected either way; CORS is a browser control, never a server-side one.
# PUBLIC_CORS_ORIGINS=https://docs.example.com,https://app.example.com

# --- What must NOT be in this file -----------------------------------------
# HELIO_WRITE_TOKEN, JAO_CORE_NET_POSITION_ENABLED, OPS_PEER_URL, COMMIT_SHA.
# `createPublicApp` throws at startup if any is set, naming the variable and
# never its value. Give them to the private app instead — it is a separate
# process with its own `.env`.
#
# ENERGY_DB_PATH is not forbidden (the key-store guard reads it to check that
# the two paths differ), but nothing in the public graph opens the energy
# database: `publicAppGraph.test.ts` asserts `config/` is unreachable from both
# entrypoints.
